From 7b3d4b53e6a62c30487d318b9bd4def479df31eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AI Developer <ai-dev@fatehmusic.local>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 18:10:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(class): add class management (Phase 3 + Phase 4)

- migrations/0021: new classes + class_students tables. Course = what
  is taught (already exists: static data/courses.js + course_overrides
  from the other course-management work, migration 0013), Class = who/
  which instructor/when (Section 9's own distinction). classes.course_id
  reuses that same id-space -- no new courses table, same pattern
  registrations.instrument_id already uses. instructor_id references
  the real instructors table (migration 0012).
- Bundled Phase 4 (Class Students, Section 10) in with Phase 3 for the
  same reason Section 8 was bundled into Phase 2: a Classes feature
  with no way to see who's enrolled isn't a usable deliverable alone.
  "a Student must not be enrolled twice in the same active Class" is
  enforced with a partial UNIQUE index (class_id, student_id) WHERE
  status='active', not just an application check -- verified directly
  against local D1 that it rejects a concurrent duplicate, and that
  withdraw-then-re-enroll still works since a withdrawn row falls
  outside the partial index.
- This is a forward-looking operational layer, intentionally NOT
  backfilled from registrations -- see migration 0021 header for why.
- src/server/classes.ts: list (search + status/instructor filter +
  pagination), full profile (class + enrolled students), create,
  update, enroll/withdraw (capacity-checked).
- src/pages/api/admin/classes.ts + class-students.ts: same
  admin/registrar gate as students/instructors.
- src/pages/admin/classes.astro (+ classes.js, class-profile.js,
  classes.css): list + create + per-class profile/edit view, with an
  enroll-student search widget that reuses the existing
  /api/admin/students search endpoint from Phase 1 rather than
  building a second student-search implementation.

Validated: npx vitest run (101/101, was 92/92 on current main) . npx
astro check (137 errors/4 hints, byte-identical to current main's
baseline once one real type error of mine -- courses.map callback
over-annotated against courses.ts's Course type -- was found and
fixed; 0 new after that) . npx astro build (clean) . full 21-migration
chain replayed from scratch locally . enrollment, the capacity/
duplicate rules, and the list/profile join queries all manually
verified against local D1 with real data.
